`world.js` line 126 `f.def.accent`; fine unless f.def undefined. Maybe scene.fighters includes something else after matchEnd? In main render: game exists, `const p = game.player; c=game.cpu`, okay.

Maybe `openMatchScreen` gets winnerKey undefined because `lastRoundWinner` got reset? Let's inspect finishRound and matchEnd logic. `lastRoundWinner` set. callback matchEnd called with this.lastRoundWinner. But in `openMatchScreen`, `const def = FIGHTERS[winnerKey]`; if winnerKey is undefined, `def` undefined, then line 366 `def.accent` => error. Why would lastRoundWinner be undefined? `startRound` doesn't reset lastRoundWinner. But in callback:
```
matchEnd: (winnerKey, info) => {
 const current = game;
 clearTimeout(matchTimer);
 matchTimer = setTimeout(() => { if (game===current...) openMatchScreen(winnerKey, info); },900);
}
```
winnerKey from `finishRound` callback? Wait matchEnd callback in game.update:
```
this.callbacks.matchEnd(this.lastRoundWinner, {...});
```
But `this.lastRoundWinner` may be a Fighter object, not a key string! In beginKO they set pendingWinner = winner object; finishRound sets `this.lastRoundWinner = winner` (object). Then callback matchEnd passes the object, and main does `FIGHTERS[winnerKey]` with object -> undefined. Yes! Also in callbacks.roundEnd they pass winner.key correctly. But matchEnd passes object. Fix: pass `this.lastRoundWinner && this.lastRoundWinner.key`. Or change callback handling to handle object. Better in game update: `this.callbacks.matchEnd(this.lastRoundWinner ? this.lastRoundWinner.key : null, ...)`. Then openMatchScreen works. Alternatively openMatchScreen robust. Also if timeUp, lastRoundWinner set. Fix.

